Now CSS:
- max-width 900: keep labels, adjust font. Replace `.title-stat span { display:none; }` with compact font & letter spacing. But maybe at 900 the footer fits; we can keep labels at all sizes. At 900 wide, labels definitely fit. So remove the display:none entirely and just tune.

```
.title-stat span { font-size: 6px; letter-spacing: 1.1px; }
.title-stat b { font-size: 16px; }
.title-footer { gap: 18px; }
```
At 620:
```
.title-footer { gap: 10px; }
.title-stat { gap: 4px; }
.title-stat span { font-size: 5.5px; letter-spacing: .7px; }
.title-stat b { font-size: 13px; }
```
And toast top 168.

Also mobile title content: ensure "ANDREAS" doesn't overflow. At 390, 18.5vw = 72px. The word's actual width? In the screenshot, "ANDREAS" starts at x 55 CSS and ends at 371 CSS (of 390) → 316px wide, with left padding 22. That fits but tight. At 360, 18.5vw=66.6, width ~292, plus 22=314, fits 360. Fine.

The play button: at mobile, min-width 240 but it spans from x 22 to 270 CSS; "ENTER THE CITY" fits. Fine.

Mobile title footer at bottom: currently `title-content` has padding-bottom 1vh and the footer maybe at the bottom. With labels restored, will it fit? Yes.

Let's apply.

